[IMP] hr_{work_entry,attendance,holidays,holidays_attendance}: sequential time rule pipeline engine

Adds a configurable threshold-based engine that automatically reclassifies
attendance and leave records when a worked-hours threshold is crossed, and
optionally creates or deducts compensatory-leave allocation credits.

MECHANISM

A rule (hr.time.rule) expresses a condition:

  "When employee X works more (or less) than Y hours on day/week D,
   reclassify the excess (or deficit) as work-entry type Z and grant
   (or deduct) N% of those hours as compensatory-leave allocation."

Rules run sequentially in sequence order. Each rule sees the already-
reclassified output of all prior rules, so they compose cleanly:

  Rule 1 - excess > 2 h -> Overtime
  Rule 2 - excess > 4 h -> Double-time   (evaluates the post-rule-1 pipeline)

KEY MODULES

hr_work_entry
  hr.time.rule           rule model, field definitions, pipeline entry point
  _evaluate_rules        builds initial intervals, runs rules in sequence,
                         extracts excess and deficit per (employee, source) pair
  _evaluate_period       period-level threshold: compares worked hours against
                         the employee's schedule or a fixed expected-hours value
  _apply_output          writes results: reclassifies sources in-place or creates
                         child output records; collects allocation credit tuples
  HrTimeRuleSourceMixin  abstract trigger layer inherited by hr.attendance and
                         hr.leave; fires the pipeline on validated create/write
                         and exposes daily/weekly cron entry points for undertime

hr_attendance
  attendance_validation  per-company policy: when an attendance counts as a
                         validated pipeline source (immediate, officer, tolerance)
  _apply_attendance_output  base implementation - no allocation tracking

hr_holidays
  leave_compensation_rate / allocation_type_id  output fields on the rule
  _apply_leave_output    excess -> hr.leave.allocation credit;
                         deficit -> allocation deduction
  hr.time.rule.allocation.log  per-source log of credits; allows precise reversal
                               when a source record is modified or deleted

hr_holidays_attendance
  bridge module: attendance-based excess/deficit also creates/deducts
  hr.leave.allocation records using the same log + reversal mechanism

TRIGGER TIMING:
  On write/create (for daily excess rules)
  Daily cron for yesterday's daily undertime
  Weekly cron for weekly rules*

* note that weekly Undertime is only processed via the weekly cron,
meaning past corrections do not trigger the weekly undertime rules.

